preConditionHook:
// The bar's open sits in the bottom nearFraction of its own high-low range
// (long) / the top nearFraction (short): little or no wick before the move
// began, Brooks's opening half of 'open on or near the low, close on or near
// the high'. The closing half is the catalog's CloseRangePosition, so only
// this half is new.
//
// Written as a product, not a quotient: EasyLanguage raises a runtime
// divide-by-zero and a zero-range bar is legal data. On such a bar
// open - low is 0 and the test passes, which is the intended reading of a
// one-price bar. CloseRangePosition takes the epsilon-quotient route instead;
// the product form is preferred here because there is no reason to divide.
//
// Not ShavedBothEndsBar, which measures both ends against an ABSOLUTE price
// offset rather than a fraction of this bar's range.
